@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] card-reader-header-is-one-row
Card reading MUST fill the screen under the status bar, as the sheet of
`card-reader-rises-as-a-sheet`, leaving only the edge of the gallery behind it showing
above. Its fixed header MUST have a 44dp Back
arrow (the reader returns to the gallery; it is not a closing action), a raised
pill with the card's name and a caret occupying the available middle width, and a
44dp Share button, which every card has since any card can be shared as an image
(`card-share-sheet-offers-what-the-card-has`). It MUST NOT add a second metadata row. Long names may ellipsize to one line in this pill, while
keeping the complete name in text semantics. The pill and controls MUST remain
separate at narrow widths and large font settings. Sheet headers remain plain
titles; this pill belongs to the reader. The card's actions moved to the foot
(`card-reader-foot-holds-its-actions`).
Source: Octavian's attached toolbar reference and one-row requirement, 22 October 2026;
the recorded review of the same day ("this icon here should actually be a back
icon"); Octavian's pick of F08 in the reader prototype, 28 October 2026, after his canvas
comment on G08 ("Maybe we can just put a share button there instead"); the sheet
instead of the whole screen from Octavian's pick of 13 and 14 on the card opening page,
30 October 2026.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design;motion] card-reader-rises-as-a-sheet
Opening a card from the gallery MUST raise the reader as a sheet with round top
corners and a grab handle, from half its height below its rest and out of a slight
blur, on the panel opening time and curve of DESIGN rule 73, while the gallery and its
bar step back behind it as one card: a little smaller from its top centre, with round
corners, under the sheets' scrim, on black. The sheet rests a little lower than the
stepped-back gallery so the gallery's edge shows above it. Back, Back to All,
Show similar, Delete card and a card removed from the space it was opened in MUST sink
the sheet the way it came, on the panel closing time, while the gallery comes forward,
and only then remove the reader. A finger MUST be able to pull the sheet down by its
header, or from the top of its content when the drag began with the content at its
top (Pully's H2, as the card's sheets do); the gallery comes forward as far as the
sheet goes down. Letting go more than 30% of the way down, or throwing it down, MUST
carry the sheet off the bottom and close the reader, as the card's sheets do (pulls.review
DESIGN rule 105); anything less springs it back to rest.
A card opened from inside the reader takes its place without the sheet moving. With
animations off, the sheet and the gallery go straight to where they end.
Source: Octavian's pick on the card opening page, 30 October 2026 ("Let's do 13 and 14
together"): 13 is transitions.dev's Panel reveal, 14 its Banner stacking; times and
curve from pulls.review DESIGN rule 73.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] card-reader-shows-the-whole-card
The reader MUST show every part of a card it has, each once, in its own raised
section: the picture (cover, post image or image file) with the title, who made it,
where it is from, when it was saved and how long its page takes to read; the post or
note body, or else the saved summary; a video file's Transcript, what the server heard
said in it (`share-takes-gallery-videos`, Octavian, 5 November 2026); the tags; the user's note; and the captured
page text with its reading time. Text sections MUST carry a small muted heading. A social
post MUST instead show as one section on its network's colour
(`gallery-posts-look-like-posts`): who posted it, with the handle, the posting day where
the post gives it and the network's mark; a Reddit post's title; its words; its picture
or video, whole; and when it was posted and saved. It shows no counts, and its title
stays in the name's pill. A Reddit post MUST show the top comments kept when it was
saved, up to three, under the post in a Top comments section, each with u/author over
its words and no points. An X post that carries an X article MUST show the article in
the post where its picture would be, as X draws it: the cover whole, the title, its
opening lines and Article on X, ruled in X's line colour; a tap opens the post on X,
where the article reads in full. A product's picture MUST carry its price as a white pill, with
its brand or shop in its byline; when the account has Same Vibe, a product's reader
shows a Same Vibe section after its words: up to three of the cards nearest it in meaning,
from the user's own library, each opening in its place. A PDF MUST show its name, PDF with
its page count and reading time once the phone has read them, and Read in Reader Mode
when it has words, then every page whole, one under another at the page's width with
"n of N" under it. The phone fetches the file from the library server once and draws
the pages itself, only those near the screen; until then the first page shows as the
server drew it.
The card's type colour MUST wash the top of the reader as a faint fade, as it does
on the card's sheets, and never tint the body. Tags are quiet pills without crosses;
the Tags section MUST NOT show Edit tags itself: Edit tags, from the tags' held
sheet, reveals a cross on each and Done hides them again, and + Add opens Add
tags. A card that is not itself a note MUST show Your note even before one is
written, inviting one. The page MUST NOT end with a line saying any part can be held.
Octavian took the always-shown Edit tags and the "Hold any part for its own actions"
line off, 4 November 2026.
Source: Octavian's recorded review, 22 October 2026 ("why is there nothing here", "can't
just tint only the bottom sheet", "some tags which look really weird"); Octavian's pick
of F08, whose page is the prototype's 02 raised sections, 28 October 2026; the post
section from Octavian's pick of X10 on the card previews canvas, 29 October 2026, and the
product's price and Same Vibe from his pick of P5 the same day, and the PDF's pages from
his pick of D5 ("I wanted to see the content"); the top comments from R4 ("the top
comments stay, from R3") and the article from XA5, both taken with "Pick recommended and
build it" the same day.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] card-reader-shows-x-threads
An X thread (`gallery-x-threads-lead-with-their-name`) MUST open with its summary in a
raised section headed What the thread says, then every kept post, oldest first, in one
section in X's black as X shows a thread: each post with a circle of the author's
initials, the name and handle, its words and its pictures whole, and a line in X's line
colour running down from each circle to the next post; then when the saved post was
posted and saved and how many posts the thread has. It shows no counts of likes or
reposts. Holding the posts' words offers the post's Copy and Share, of every post's
words; a picture opens the post on X. The server keeps only posts written before the
saved one, because the posts after it need X's paid API.
Source: Octavian's pick of 08 Summary first on the X threads page, 4 November 2026 ("Let's
implement 08").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] card-reader-opens-its-source
A card with a web link MUST open it from a tap on its picture and from the foot's
Open source pill, which speaks the site's name. Holding the picture MUST open its
own sheet (`card-reader-parts-are-held`). A card without a link MUST NOT show Open
source; a PDF without one shows Open the PDF in its place, which hands the file to the
phone's own viewer. A video the server
keeps plays in place instead (`card-reader-plays-videos`), and Open source still
opens its link.
Source: Octavian's recorded review, 22 October 2026 ("especially the preview, I should be
taken to the source"); Octavian's pick of F08, 28 October 2026; Open the PDF from his pick of
D5 on the card previews canvas, 29 October 2026.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] card-reader-foot-holds-its-actions
The reader's foot MUST float Open source (or Open the PDF), a 52dp pill in the page's ink, and a 52dp
