@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] card-reader-parts-are-held
Holding a part of the reader MUST open a sheet titled with the part's name that
offers only what that part has: the picture offers Save picture (its file when it
has one, else the picture as drawn), Copy picture and Share picture; a summary, post or note offers Copy and
Share; Tags offers Edit tags and Copy tags; Your note offers Write a note, or Edit
note and Copy note; the page text offers Read in Reader Mode and Copy text. Edit
tags closes the sheet and shows the tags' crosses (`card-reader-shows-the-whole-card`;
a card without tags opens Add tags in the same sheet), Edit note opens its page in
the same sheet, and Your note saves with
Done, an emptied note taking the note off. Each hold MUST also be offered to
accessibility services as an action.
Source: Octavian's pick of F08 in the reader prototype, 28 October 2026 (M20, hold a
part for a small menu with few options). Save picture for every picture, not only
picture files, follows Octavian's 6 November 2026 ask that pictures "be able to be copied,
and downloaded. Both single and multi".

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] card-reader-mode
Reader Mode MUST show only the page's text, selectable and at the reading size,
under the card's title and byline, ending with Back to the card. The foot hides and
the name's pill draws a thin line that fills as the text is read. The header's Back
and system Back MUST return to the card rather than close it. Reader Mode opens from
Choose one and from the page text's sheet, for any card with page text, and from a
PDF's Read in Reader Mode with the words the phone reads from its pages (Android 15 and
later), joined back into paragraphs.
Source: Octavian's pick of F08 in the reader prototype, 28 October 2026 (M27, Reader
Mode, "definitely"); PDFs from his pick of D5 on the card previews canvas, 29 October 2026.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design;motion] card-reader-name-grows-into-its-card
Tapping the reader's name MUST grow its pill into a card of the card's details over
a light scrim: its picture beside who made it, where it is from, when it was saved
and its reading time; then Copy link (only for a card with a link), Pin as a
switch, and Spaces naming the card's spaces; then up to three cards opened before
it, each of which opens in its place, and Back to All. Copy link and Spaces
hide the card before they act; Pin keeps it open. Tapping the name, the scrim
or system Back MUST shrink it back into the pill before Back closes the reader.
