@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design;motion] card-reader-plays-videos
A video the library server keeps MUST open in the reader as a video player, as Google
Photos does: it starts by itself with sound over its still, a tap on the video pauses
or resumes it, and under it sit play or pause, the time played of the whole, sound on
or off, and a bar to move through it. It MUST pause when the app leaves the screen and
stop when the reader closes, and it MUST only request media from the library server.
Videos on other sites keep their still picture, which opens the source.
Source: Octavian's recorded review, 23 October 2026 ("we should be showing things like kind
of more similar to how Google Photos shows a video", "they open kind of a video player,
which makes far more sense for a video").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] card-reader-beside-the-gallery
On an unfolded window (window-shapes-follow-pully) the reader MUST show in the pane beside
the gallery, fading in and out instead of rising as a sheet, with no grab handle or pull to
close, and its header MUST leave Back out, because the gallery it would go back to is in
sight; Reader Mode keeps its Back to the card, and system Back still closes the reader. On
