@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design;motion] card-reader-plays-audio
An audio file the library server keeps MUST open in the reader with a compact player above
the title: a round play or pause button, a bar the person can drag to move through the
file, and the time played of the whole. It MUST wait to be played rather than start by
itself, pause when the app leaves the screen and release its player when the reader
closes, and it MUST only request media from the library server. The card's Transcript
MUST show as a part of the reader, held like the other parts (card-reader-parts-are-held),
once the server has transcribed the file.
Source: Octavian, 5 Nov 2026: "If we're not already using this for audio too, then we
definitely should be".
